  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the figure given below. a block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>490</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;placed on a frictionless table is connected with two springs having same spring constant (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>). If the block is horizontally displaced through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> then the number of complete oscillations it will make in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math> seconds will be ______.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/def3d0ba-9e6a-4709-805f-bdce7f881a7a-9896057.PNG\" style=\"width: 343px; height: 225px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b1fba8f3-a42b-4208-93ad-459d2ef403a8-9896057_1.PNG\" style=\"width: 326px; height: 70px;\" /></p><p>Both the springs are connected in parallel, therefore</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></math></p><p>Now, time period of spring-block system is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>490</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>49</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mn>49</mn><mn>400</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, number of oscillation in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>time</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
